/-
# Locally finite groups with a finite centralizer (Kourovka Notebook Problem 4.76)

Kourovka Notebook, Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 4.76 (V. P. Shunkov): let G be a locally
finite group containing an element a of prime order such that the centralizer C_G(a) is finite; is G
almost soluble?
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.OrderOfElement
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.Solvable
public import WantedExt.GroupTheory.GroupClassesShared

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.FiniteCentralizerAlmostSolubleKourovka4Problem76Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 4.76 (V. P.
Shunkov). UnsolvedMath record UM-00700283 (`KOU-4.76`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

Locally finite (the subgroup generated by every finite set is finite) is `IsLocallyFinite` of
`GroupClassesShared`; almost soluble means having a soluble subgroup of finite index. The Archive
adds that `G` is even almost nilpotent (Khukhro); the target states the question as asked.
-/

open MathlibExt.GroupTheory.GroupClassesShared (IsLocallyFinite)

/-- Kourovka 4.76 (V. P. Shunkov): a locally finite group `G` containing an element `a` of prime
order with finite centralizer `C_G(a)` is almost soluble: it has a soluble subgroup of finite
index. -/
def finiteCentralizerAlmostSoluble : Prop :=
  ∀ (G : Type) [Group G], IsLocallyFinite G → ∀ a : G, (orderOf a).Prime →
    (Subgroup.centralizer {a} : Set G).Finite → ∃ H : Subgroup G, H.FiniteIndex ∧ Group.IsSolvable H

/--
Resolved true: the Kourovka Archive answers 4.76 "Yes, it is": by Fong (mod CFSG) such a group is
almost locally soluble, by Hartley and Meixner almost locally nilpotent, and by Alperin and Higman
almost soluble; by Khukhro it is even almost nilpotent. Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov
(eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49
(2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 4.76 (V. P. Shunkov); resolution: P. Fong, Osaka J.
Math. 13 (1976), 483-489; B. Hartley and T. Meixner, Arch. Math. 36 (1981), 211-213; J. L. Alperin,
Proc. Amer. Math. Soc. 13 (1962), 175-180; G. Higman, J. London Math. Soc. 32 (1957), 321-334,
Kourovka Archive, Problem 4.76: Yes, it is: Fong showed (mod CFSG) that G is almost locally soluble,
Hartley and Meixner then proved G almost locally nilpotent, and G is almost soluble by Alperin and
Higman, https://arxiv.org/abs/1401.0300v49.
-/
public theorem_wanted finiteCentralizerAlmostSoluble_holds : finiteCentralizerAlmostSoluble

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.FiniteCentralizerAlmostSolubleKourovka4Problem76Wanted
